# Wave W17-P (Route 117): day turf — field green under the flower beds: a bright, open field green with pale petal-fall flecks drifting off the beds the Day-Care fence keeps (design: calm speckled grass through ordered flower fields; the shipped flower beds stand byte-preserved as the route’s dressing and the ground converts around them). Route 117’s own ground — the loudest green in the tranche, split from Route 116’s hushed sage at a glance (field sun vs hill shade) and from Route 104’s bed turf by register: these fields are worked and fenced, not roadside beds.
